Patch from MiniMyth2 project

Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>



From 59eb89c10008f3c49568ecb9b5ea3ad07f117b00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:41:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: rockchip: Don't put an error pointer on clock
 lookup failure

When a clock of a power domain cannot be looked up yet, e.g. because
the CRU is a platform driver that has not probed yet, the error path
calls clk_bulk_put() on all the clocks of the domain, including the
error pointer returned by of_clk_get(). This triggers the
WARN_ON_ONCE(IS_ERR(clk)) in __clk_put() on every boot of the RK3528,
for a perfectly normal probe deferral.

Clear the failed entry before putting the clocks, so that only the
clocks that were actually obtained are put, and use dev_err_probe() so
that the probe deferral is no longer reported as an error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
index e193f97..7351eb4 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
@@ -851,9 +851,11 @@ static int rockchip_pm_add_one_domain(struct rockchip_pmu *pmu,
 		pd->clks[i].clk = of_clk_get(node, i);
 		if (IS_ERR(pd->clks[i].clk)) {
 			error = PTR_ERR(pd->clks[i].clk);
-			dev_err(pmu->dev,
-				"%pOFn: failed to get clk at index %d: %d\n",
-				node, i, error);
+			/* Don't let clk_bulk_put() put the error pointer */
+			pd->clks[i].clk = NULL;
+			dev_err_probe(pmu->dev, error,
+				      "%pOFn: failed to get clk at index %d\n",
+				      node, i);
 			goto err_put_clocks;
 		}
 	}
@@ -1006,8 +1008,8 @@ static int rockchip_pm_add_subdomain(struct rockchip_pmu *pmu,
 
 		error = rockchip_pm_add_one_domain(pmu, np);
 		if (error) {
-			dev_err(pmu->dev, "failed to handle node %pOFn: %d\n",
-				np, error);
+			dev_err_probe(pmu->dev, error,
+				      "failed to handle node %pOFn\n", np);
 			return error;
 		}
 
@@ -1102,8 +1104,8 @@ static int rockchip_pm_domain_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	for_each_available_child_of_node_scoped(np, node) {
 		error = rockchip_pm_add_one_domain(pmu, node);
 		if (error) {
-			dev_err(dev, "failed to handle node %pOFn: %d\n",
-				node, error);
+			dev_err_probe(dev, error, "failed to handle node %pOFn\n",
+				      node);
 			goto err_out;
 		}
 
